To prevent unhandled process crashes when critical validation files are missing or malformed, we should wrap the file loading in a try-catch block. If loading fails, we can record a critical file load failure diagnostic, initialize empty mock inputs to allow the pipeline to complete safely, and ensure the validator fails closed. This aligns with the repository's general rules on loading critical validation files.

```javascript
export function buildFullBetaRuntimeSourceMap(options = {}) {
  const root = options.root ?? repoRootFromScript();
  const paths = { ...DEFAULT_PATHS, ...(options.paths ?? {}) };
  const generatedAt = options.generatedAt ?? DEFAULT_GENERATED_AT;

  const diagnostics = [];
  let inputs;
  try {
    inputs = options.inputs ?? loadInputs(root, paths);
  } catch (error) {
    diagnostics.push({
      type: 'critical_file_load_failure',
      reason: error.message,
      stack: error.stack,
    });
    inputs = {
      plainTextV2: { items: [] },
      consumption: { items: [] },
      fullDataGovernanceFinalGate: { final_counts: {} },
      sourceDocumentRegistry: { registry: [] },
      historicalCropRiskAudit: { rows: [] },
    };
  }

  const plainTextItems = asArray(inputs.plainTextV2.items);
  const consumptionItems = asArray(inputs.consumption.items);
  const sourceRegistryRows = asArray(inputs.sourceDocumentRegistry.registry);
  const cropRiskRows = asArray(inputs.historicalCropRiskAudit.rows);
  const rows = buildRows({
    plainTextItems,
    consumptionItems,
    sourceRegistryRows,
    cropRiskRows,
    paths,
    generatedAt,
    diagnostics,
  });
  const summary = buildSummary(rows, inputs.plainTextV2.summary, inputs.consumption.summary, inputs.finalGate);
```

